From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:44:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 036/342] arm64: VMSAv8TranslationMap: no page table to free
 for an unused map

The page table is allocated with the first mapping. When fork_team()
failed before mapping anything (low memory), deleting the new address
space freed page table 0 and faulted on physical address 0 in the
kernel: a panic instead of a failed fork.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/VMSAv8TranslationMap.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/VMSAv8TranslationMap.cpp b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/VMSAv8TranslationMap.cpp
index c4ca593238..5512b8e98e 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/VMSAv8TranslationMap.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/VMSAv8TranslationMap.cpp
@@ -151,9 +151,13 @@ VMSAv8TranslationMap::~VMSAv8TranslationMap()
 		}
 	}
 
-	vm_page_reservation reservation = {};
-	FreeTable(fPageTable, 0, fInitialLevel, &reservation);
-	vm_page_unreserve_pages(&reservation);
+	// The page table is only allocated with the first mapping: a map whose
+	// address space never got one (a fork that failed early) has none.
+	if (fPageTable != 0) {
+		vm_page_reservation reservation = {};
+		FreeTable(fPageTable, 0, fInitialLevel, &reservation);
+		vm_page_unreserve_pages(&reservation);
+	}
 }
 
 
